<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.01920v1/openagi_react_prompt_vs_time.svg" id="S5.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:210/125;" width="210" height="125"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S5.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt Token Increase vs Time Decrease</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.01920v1/openagi_react_gen_vs_time.svg" id="S5.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:210/125;" width="210" height="125"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S5.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Generation Token Increase vs Time Decrease</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance trade-off between acceleration and token increase between Fix-<math id="S5.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, Dynamic-<math id="S5.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and Dynamic-offset SP. (a) Prompt token and (b) Generation token increase vs. latency reduction, both relative to a normal-plan baseline.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S5.T1" title="In 5.2 Main Experiment Result ‣ 5 Main Experiment ‣ Dynamic Speculative Agent Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#S5.T2" title="In 5.2 Main Experiment Result ‣ 5 Main Experiment ‣ Dynamic Speculative Agent Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#S5.T3" title="In 5.2 Main Experiment Result ‣ 5 Main Experiment ‣ Dynamic Speculative Agent Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.2 Main Experiment Result ‣ 5 Main Experiment ‣ Dynamic Speculative Agent Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, our experiments validate that DSP achieves superior Pareto efficiency compared to fixed-k baselines. Key findings include:</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.1 </span>Cost-Efficiency Dominance</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DSP demonstrates <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict Pareto dominance</span> through two operational modes:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Equivalent Latency, Lower Cost</span> <em id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">On the OpenAGI benchmark</em>:
In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 1</span>, Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>) and Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{offset}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>offset</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{offset}=2</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves comparable time reduction to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=6</annotation></semantics></math>) with a <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">34.9%</span> (1.25<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> compared with 1.92<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> as in <a href="#S5.T1" title="In 5.2 Main Experiment Result ‣ 5 Main Experiment ‣ Dynamic Speculative Agent Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) reduction in cost.
Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{offset}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>offset</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{offset}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) saved <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">23.4%</span> total cost compared to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math>) with comparable latency reduction.
Compared to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>), Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves a similar latency reduction and a substantial 12% decrease in token cost.
In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 2</span>: Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves comparable latency reduction to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math>) while saving 9.49% cost. Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{offset}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>offset</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{offset}=2</annotation></semantics></math>) yields a marginally better acceleration than Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=6</annotation></semantics></math>), and significantly reduces token cost by <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">28.25%</span>.
In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 3</span>: Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>) and Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{offset}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>offset</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{offset}=2</annotation></semantics></math>) saves 6.78% and 10.67 % cost compared to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math>) with a marginal acceleration improvement.
In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 4</span>: Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>) saves 7.38% cost compared to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math>) with comparable latency reduction.
<em id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">On the Travel Planner benchmark</em>: Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves a 7% reduction in cost in <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 1</span>, along with modest latency improvements compared to Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Equivalent Cost, Faster Execution</span> <em id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">On the OpenAGI benchmark</em>: In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 1</span>, Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>) delivers 5% relative acceleration over Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>), only consuming 2% more cost.
In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 2</span>, Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) provides 8% better latency reduction while consuming 5% less cost than Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>).
In <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">setting 4</span>, Dyn. (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{offset}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>offset</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{offset}=2</annotation></semantics></math>) requires 9.52% fewer cost to surpass Fix (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">DSP consistently outperforms all fixed-<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> baselines in terms of cost-effective acceleration in all the settings evaluated. In our experiments on multiple benchmarks and model pairings, DSP achieves strictly computational cost for equal or lower latency compared to any static speculation policy. We provide a comprehensive analysis of unnecessary cost reduction and time acceleration relative to sequential planning in <a href="#S5.SS2.SSS2" title="5.2.2 Actual Performance ‣ 5.2 Main Experiment Result ‣ 5 Main Experiment ‣ Dynamic Speculative Agent Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2.2</span></a>. The experiment results also show that DSP yields consistent benefits across different agent configurations and benchmarks, demonstrating the adaptability of our approach.
This generality underscores that a learned dynamic scheduling policy can effectively identify and exploit parallelism opportunities in a variety of reasoning pipelines.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.2 </span>Actual Performance</h4>

